From 40dbbf68c63993bf621cfd3fb097c91452145a0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:18:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homar settings icon: a "Homa Lawn" icon in the app drawer
 opens the settings

An activity-alias of PreferenceActivity (MAIN/LAUNCHER only, never HOME) with the app's own icon
and name, like Nova's "Nova Settings". Upstream hides its own package from search results, so
SettingsIcon lets this one alias through (one-line hook in LawnchairSearchAlgorithm).

The launcher's home entry was meant to be hidden from the drawer by filtered_components, but that
list says app.lawnchair/... without the debug build's ".debug" suffix, so it showed as a second
"Homa Lawn" that only went home. SettingsIcon.isHomeEntry hides it by the real package name (hook
in AppFilter), which also keeps it out of launcher.apps_list for the desktop editor.

launcher.app_icons lists the same apps as launcher.apps_list (through AppFilter), so
the desktop editor gets no icon for the hidden home entry either.
